WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.563
I have to ask you about this.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.860
I see it every day I come here.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.424
It's a crocheted pillow,

00:00:06.424 --> 00:00:07.590
(Sarah chuckles)

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.700
with the face of you Sarah Silverman,

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.940
and it's here,

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.820
we've had it steam cleaned because,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.410
well that's just what you do with anything

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.640
that's been sitting around the Largo.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.450
What is the story-
So many people have sat,

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.567
I'm sure it's covered in fecal
matter and like dried semen.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:22.800
[Conan] Yeah.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.549
I mean it's a little distorted.

00:00:24.549 --> 00:00:26.210
Well first of all,

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.830
why is there a crocheted pillow

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.370
with your face on it here at Largo?

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.203
Explain.

00:00:31.203 --> 00:00:32.997
That needs an explanation?
Yes, it does.

00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:34.763
No, it does have an explanation.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.723
About five years ago I think,

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.634
I won't go into the whole
story but I almost died.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:43.827
I remember this.
Randomly.

00:00:43.827 --> 00:00:45.840
You had a medical emergency yes.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.910
Yeah. I had like a thing,

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.590
abscess on the top of my windpipe

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.759
it was either gonna choke me to death

00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:57.010
or poison me to death if it exploded.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.540
It's just one of those crazy things.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.520
I had a surgery where they told my manager

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.710
and my boyfriend at the time

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.312
it was like 50-50 chance of survival.

00:01:04.312 --> 00:01:07.270
[Conan] Oh my God.
But I am fine.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:11.920
But I was in an induced coma for a week.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.920
And my other friend named
Coco, Mark Coco Cohen,

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.530
he didn't know what to do with himself

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.490
he felt so helpless.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.040
And he crochets,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.660
and as matter of fact when
he first started crocheting

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.363
he crocheted a huge blanket,

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.390
he felt emasculated by his new passion,

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.877
so he wrote the word
twat in the middle of it.

00:01:39.877 --> 00:01:42.009
Just like a huge crocheted anyway.

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:43.957
You know grandma Moses
made a lot of those.

00:01:43.957 --> 00:01:44.790
(laughs)

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.640
Yeah such a sweet...

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.690
Look check out, look for that on Etsy.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:54.310
But-
So he was so,

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.160
he didn't know what to do with himself,

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.100
so he crocheted a pillow
with my face on it.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:01:59.933
And then when I got out of the hospital

00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:02.250
he gave it to me and it meant so much

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:07.020
'cause I knew it just was made with love.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.194
But then, I live in this little apartment.

00:02:09.194 --> 00:02:10.383
[Conan] Right.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.203
I was with Flanigan,

00:02:12.203 --> 00:02:14.799
and I go, I love Mark so much
and I love that he made this,

00:02:14.799 --> 00:02:17.160
but I can't have a
pillow with my face on it

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.080
in my three-room apartment.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.670
And he said, "Bring it on down to."

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.503
I can't do accents.

00:02:23.503 --> 00:02:25.542
Ah, bring it on down to the theater!

00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:26.578
(both laugh)

00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:27.962
Bring it on down to Largo.
[Man] Watch out for the Row

00:02:27.962 --> 00:02:29.060
and El Duce heads.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.920
(Conan chuckles)

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.140
We kick it around like a Mussolini head.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.880
You see that's what everybody
does with the stuff they are

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.850
too embarrassed to have in their house.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.650
There's an oil painting
of Zach Galifianakis,

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:46.073
and Jeff Garlin painting,
and everyone just brings

00:02:46.073 --> 00:02:47.200
it's ink source.
Right.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.360
'Cause they don't want to throw it out,

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.020
but they can't have it in their home.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.750
Right. If it means a great deal to you,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.520
which you wanted to sit
in an abandoned theater,

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.375
bring it to Largo.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.040
(both chuckle)

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.953
I think that's a Fiona Apple song.

00:02:58.953 --> 00:03:00.020
Where the Tidal love her.
It probably is.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.270
It should be if it isn't.

